+++ b/CHANGES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+No traces this round (`traces/` did not exist). Hardened `parseCsvLine`
+against the contract in README.md § Contract directly.
+
+### src/csv.mjs
+
+Rewrote `parseCsvLine` as a single index-based pass (`charCodeAt` /
+`indexOf` / `slice` on ranges). The previous version re-sliced the remaining
+string on every character, which was quadratic; the new one is linear
+(5 MB inputs of every shape parse in well under 200 ms).
+
+Contract rules implemented:
+
+- Non-string argument throws `TypeError` (unchanged, kept).
+- Only `string[]` or `CsvError` comes out for any string input.
+- Fields separated by `,`; `""` -> `[""]`; `a,` -> `["a", ""]`.
+- Quoted fields; `""` inside quotes is one `"`; commas, `\n`, `\r\n` (and
+  lone `\r`) are literal inside quotes.
+- After a closing quote only `,`, the trailing record terminator or the end
+  of text may follow; anything else is a `CsvError`.
+- Unclosed quoted field is a `CsvError`.
+- A `"` anywhere in an unquoted field is a `CsvError` (`a"b`, `a "b"`, `a"`).
+- Whitespace outside quotes is preserved.
+- Exactly one `\n` or `\r\n` at the very end of the text is removed; any
+  other unquoted `\r` or `\n` is a `CsvError` (`a\r`, `a\n\n`, `a\nb`, ...).
+- Every other character (tabs, NUL, control chars, NEL/LS/PS, BOM, lone
+  surrogates, any Unicode) is literal.
+
+### tests/csv.test.mjs
+
+One test per contract rule (16 tests), plus:
+
+- a fuzz test over the alphabet `a , " \n \r space tab` (5000 strings)
+  asserting only `string[]` or `CsvError` ever comes out;
+- a 100 KB timing test covering one large unquoted field, one large quoted
+  field, 34 K small fields, 100 K empty fields, a field of 50 K escaped
+  quotes, 25 K quoted fields, 50 K quoted `\r\n`, and three error paths, each
+  asserted under 1 s.
+
+### Traces fixed
+
+None (round 0 had no traces).
